---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";

const UPDATED = "12 November 2026";
---

<Site
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms for using the Mzizi websites, API, MCP server and Claude plugin."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede={`Last updated ${UPDATED}. How you may use what Mzizi publishes, and what we do not promise.`}
>
  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    These terms cover <code>mzizi.dev</code>, <code>docs.mzizi.dev</code>,{" "}
    <code>api.mzizi.dev</code>, <code>mcp.mzizi.dev</code> and the Mzizi Claude plugin. They sit
    under the Bundu Foundation's <a href="https://www.bundu.org/legal/terms">terms of use</a>,
    which apply where this page is silent. The console at <code>app.mzizi.dev</code> is run by
    Nyuchi Africa (Pvt) Ltd, whose <a href="https://www.nyuchi.com/legal/terms">terms</a> apply
    to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Using what we publish</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    The websites, the registry API and the free MCP tools are open to read with no account. The
    public source code, the components and the design tokens are licensed under Apache-2.0; each
    repository carries the licence file that governs it. You may use the API and the MCP server
    in your own tools. They are rate limited, and we may slow or refuse a client that harms the
    service for others.
  </p>

  <h2>Mzizi is a research prototype</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    The Mzizi language is in Phase 0. This site says what is built and what is only designed, and
    the language's own tracker is the record. Nothing here is a promise of speed, fitness for a
    purpose or availability. The APIs and the MCP tools can change, and a component's contract
    can change between versions.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Everything is provided as it is, without warranty of any kind, to the extent the law allows.
    Check what you rely on against the source: every claim on this site traces to a file in the
    open repositories or to a request you can make yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Names and marks</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Mzizi, Bundu, Nyuchi, Mukoko and Shamwari are names and marks of their owners within the
    Bundu ecosystem. The Apache-2.0 licence does not grant the right to use them to suggest
    endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:support@bundu.org">support@bundu.org</a>.
    Security reports: <a href="mailto:security@nyuchi.com">security@nyuchi.com</a>. See also the{" "}
    <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
</Site>
